# KNOWN GAP — SILENT WRONG-CODE, both lanes, `gg check` clean.
# MUST EXCLUDE from any bulk `gg fmt` sweep: this fixture's SUBJECT is the
# pattern SPELLING. `gg fmt` at HEAD rewrites `case Satx():` -> `case Satx:`,
# which swaps the AST node kind (Constructor -> Binding) and destroys the cell.
#
# A `case` arm naming something that does not exist silently becomes a
# CATCH-ALL that kills every arm below it. Here the FIRST arm names `Satx`,
# which is not a variant of `Day` — so on Rust gg both `Mon` and `Sat` are
# swallowed and two live arms are dead, while `gg check` reports
# "OK: no semantic errors".
#
# Measured at HEAD (2026-08-16), scrutinee returned from a function so nothing
# const-folds:
#     gg check  -> OK: no semantic errors        (rc 0, no warning of any kind)
#     Rust gg   -> typo-arm / typo-arm           (Mon AND Sat both swallowed)
#     ggdef     -> mon-arm / sat-arm             (the bogus arm never matches)
# One accepted program, two different behaviours => Core #8, >= 2 bugs.
#
# INTENDED (ratified 2026-08-16, docs/define-gorget/decisions.md): this program
# is REJECTED at check time, by either ratified rule —
#   (1) UNREACHABLE-ARM: the arms after the catch-all are unreachable; and
#   (2) BARE/CONSTRUCTOR NAME ON AN ENUM SCRUTINEE MUST RESOLVE: `Satx` is not
#       a variant of `Day`, and the diagnostic points at `else:` for a catch-all.
# Bindings stay legal where they mean something: `case Custom(r, g, b):`
# destructuring and `case x if pred(x):` guards are unaffected.
#
# Wired test: known_gap_case_unresolved_name_rejected (tests/integration.rs,
# #[ignore]d). It asserts the REJECTION, so it fails today and goes green when
# the ratified rules land.
enum Day:
    Mon()
    Sat()

Day pick(int n):
    if n == 0:
        return Day.Mon()
    return Day.Sat()

String label(Day d):
    match d:
        case Satx():
            return "typo-arm"
        case Mon():
            return "mon-arm"
        case Sat():
            return "sat-arm"
        else:
            return "else-arm"

void main():
    print(label(pick(0)))
    print(label(pick(1)))
